    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0137" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.0141 Phoenix Group/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lindsay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 223</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-16">July 16, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to inform you that the
                    attention of His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom has been drawn to
                    the recent visit to Canton Island of the United States minesweeper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Avocet</hi>, of which no prior official communication
                    was made. I have accordingly been instructed to transmit to you herewith, for
                    the information of the United States Government, the enclosed copy of an Order
                    in Council of the 13th [<hi rendition="#italic">18th</hi>] March, 1937,<anchor
                        n="28" xml:id="d87-f1"/> by which Canton Island and the other islands in the
                    Phoenix Group were incorporated in the Gilbert and Ellice Islands Colony.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>R. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lindsay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
